# SEC-001 depends on these two lines. `fetch-secrets.sh` writes real credentials
# here on every container start, and a commit that carries them is the failure
# the whole secrets gate exists to prevent — one that no scanner can undo once
# it reaches a remote.
#
# Keep this file in the copy you make. Deleting it does not fail a build; it
# fails quietly, later, in someone else's clone.
.env
.env.docker
